DEPOSITION OF: eleven-sons.trial.

OFF THE RECORD: Eleven sons, born in one order, filed in another.
OFF THE RECORD: The roster is alphabetical, so the eighth is heard
OFF THE RECORD: first and the third is heard last, and no one asked
OFF THE RECORD: the sons.

EXPECT PROCLAMATION: "I have 11 sons.".
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the eighth: my child of sorrow, who keeps his distance.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the eleventh: delicate, but the delicacy is a kind of strength.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the fifth: kind, and impossible to praise.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the first: handsome, but a trifle shallow.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the fourth: open-hearted; one worries.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the ninth: elegant, with the wrong friends.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the second: at home in the world, and it shows.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the seventh: witty in a way the age rejects.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the sixth: thoughtful, or at least stooped.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the tenth: so earnest he is suspected of irony.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: the third: beautiful, and not to my taste.
EXPECT PROCLAMATION: "These are my eleven sons. The Court has filed them in its own order; so, I suppose, have I.".
EXPECT ADJOURNMENT.
